From: emscripten-forge
Subject: [PATCH] Direct calls with the callee's signature

WebAssembly requires every call to match the type of the function it
calls; natively, extra or missing arguments and an ignored result go
unnoticed. Declarations and calls now match the definitions:
- C/C++ declarations of Fortran subroutines (Scilab's, BLAS, LAPACK,
  ARPACK, SLICOT) return void, not int or double;
- C/C++ calls to Fortran routines pass the hidden lengths of CHARACTER
  arguments (1 for the one-letter options), and their declarations list
  them (long int); C functions called by Fortran with a CHARACTER
  argument take its length (addfile, colnewmsgs);
- C functions Fortran calls as subroutines return void (basout, cvstr,
  error, rk4, rpoly, ...); readf/writef use clunit as the function it is;
- no extra arguments: dpodiv, writedoubleszscfile, dseupd (no length for
  the LOGICAL rvec), getObjectFromHandle's no-graphics stub;
- feq/feqn, passed as arguments, have explicit interfaces (and arl2's t
  is double precision); icse passes icse2 the three names it takes;
- relvar's dummy arguments went past column 72 (izag and iter were one);
- dlamch is declared double precision where implicit typing made it REAL;
- riccpack's DLASD2 (a Sylvester solver) is renamed RICSD2: in a static
  link it replaced LAPACK's DLASD2, called by DLASD1.
(scicos.c's declarations are fixed in 0007, with its other call types.)
